course: dictionary
lesson: 14459
title: Parentage: who your parents are
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Parentage is a slightly formal word with two meanings. The first is who your parents are. «The hero's parentage was a secret until the final chapter» means nobody knew who the hero's parents were.
explain: The second meaning is your origin: the family or country your parents come from. «Sam is of Irish parentage» means his parents come from Ireland. Look for clue words such as parents, family, country or come from.
explain: Parentage is usually uncountable, so we say «her parentage», not «her parentages». Phrases such as «of mixed parentage» and «unknown parentage» are worth learning as whole chunks.
explain: In science, a plant's or animal's parentage is the parents it was bred from. «The puppy's parentage was a collie and a poodle» tells you which two dogs were its parents.
fact: Parentage means who your parents are, or the family or country they come from.
fact: «Parentage» is a formal word, so you will meet it more in stories and writing than in everyday talk.
fact: Useful phrases: «of mixed parentage», «of Irish parentage», «unknown parentage».
fact: In science, parentage means which parents a plant or animal was bred from.
exercise: «The hero's parentage was a secret until the final chapter.» What does parentage mean here? | How tall the hero was | *Who the hero's parents were | The hero's favourite food | The hero's best friend
exercise: Sam's family came from Ireland, so Sam is of Irish parentage. What does parentage mean in this sentence? | His favourite colour | *The country his parents come from | The name of his school | How old he is
exercise: Which word means who your parents are? | *parentage | parrot | parade | parcel
test: «Mia is of mixed parentage: her mum comes from Nigeria and her dad comes from Scotland.» What does mixed parentage tell you? | She has two pets | Her parents are twins | Her hair is two colours | *Her parents come from different countries
test: In a science book: «The plant's parentage was two different roses.» What does parentage mean here? | *The two parents the plant was bred from | The colour of its leaves | How quickly it grows | The place where it was planted
exam: Which sentence uses parentage correctly? | *«Her parentage is Greek, so her grandparents came from Greece.» | «He parentaged three cakes before the party.» | «We ate parentage for lunch on Sunday.» | «The parentage was loud and played football.»
